# Play with less motion
@scenario office_lesson_29
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg office]
[char pip global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show pip desk neutral]
pip: Some readers prefer an uninterrupted, still frame. A visual cue should remain understandable without motion.
pip: Use reduced motion on the project board, then replay the camera and transition lessons.
> Compare reduced motion -> preview_still
> Try the checkpoint -> check
@label preview_still
[if tutorial_still]
pip: I stay at my desk and use a pointing pose. You can change this in Progress and motion on the board.
[else]
[move pip desk stride-a-right exprdur=0]
[move pip window ease_in_out_cubic 620]
[wait 150]
[move pip window stride-b-right exprdur=0]
[wait 150]
[move pip window stride-c-right exprdur=0]
[wait 150]
[move pip window stride-b-right exprdur=0]
[wait 170]
[move pip window point exprdur=90]
pip: Watch the window mark. In reduced motion, I give this cue from my desk.
[move pip window stride-a-left exprdur=0]
[move pip desk ease_out_cubic 500]
[wait 120]
[move pip desk stride-b-left exprdur=0]
[wait 120]
[move pip desk stride-c-left exprdur=0]
[wait 120]
[move pip desk stride-b-left exprdur=0]
[wait 140]
[move pip desk neutral exprdur=90]
[endif]
[jump check]
@label check
pip: What must remain available in still mode?
> The same story and navigation. -> correct
> Only the title screen. -> retry
@label retry
[show pip desk curious]
pip: Optional motion should never gate information or progress. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show pip desk cheer]
pip: Optional motion should never gate information or progress.
> Finish this lesson -> return_hub
> Try the lesson again -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_29]
[flag tutorial_done_29]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_6]
